  "_comment": "Keyboard source -> NAOMI, through OpenJVS on the Pi. Button names are JVS's own, as OpenJVS's 'generic' game map uses them: an 8-way lever, BUTTON_1..6 and START. They are deliberately unlabelled beyond their numbers, because what BUTTON_1 does is per game, not per console. COIN, TEST and SERVICE are NOT here and are not buttons: a coin goes in a slot and test/service live inside the coin door, so they are cabinet events, not player controls. They belong to the target, not to whatever source is driving the game.",
